# Standard secret access: `secret` and the envelope surface.
#
# Disposition: EXECUTING. Both tools read an environment-backed secret
# through the runtime's `secrets::SecretRuntime` with a replay-safe
# trace contract.
#
# `secret(name)` is the one to use. It returns a `Secret`, which the
# program can compare with `==` (in constant time) and pass to the
# tools that need it, and which the compiler keeps out of every place
# its text could leave the program: it cannot be printed, turned into
# a `String`, encoded as JSON, stored, or passed to a prompt. A tool
# that takes a `Secret` receives the text, and every record of the
# call (the trace, approvals, replay) holds `<redacted>` in that
# position. A missing variable is an `Err`.
#
# `secret_read(name)` returns the text as a plain `String` inside an
# envelope, for programs that must handle the text themselves. Prefer
# `secret`: a `String` can reach a log, a prompt or another tool's
# trace, which a `Secret` cannot.
#
# For both:
#
#   - The PROGRAM receives the real value.
#   - The TRACE never does: the recorded ToolResult carries a
#     redacted copy (`secret` records `<redacted>`; `secret_read`
#     sets `value_redacted: true` and replaces the value with the
#     `<redacted:..>` marker). Traces must never persist secret
#     values.
#   - REPLAY re-executes the env read instead of substituting from
#     the trace — the same read-passthrough rule `db_query` follows
#     (env reads are process-internal inputs; they cannot escape).
#     If the environment differs at replay time, the run diverges
#     HONESTLY instead of replaying a value the trace never stored.

import "./effects" use EffectEnvelope, effect_envelope

public type SecretReadEnvelope:
    name: String
    present: Bool
    value: String
    value_redacted: Bool
    effect_meta: EffectEnvelope

public effect secrets_read:
    reversible: true

# The secret named `name` from the environment. An empty name, an
# unreadable variable and a missing variable are Err values, because
# there is no `Secret` to return.
public tool secret(name: String) -> Result<Secret, String> uses secrets_read

# Recoverable failures (empty name, unreadable variable) are Err
# VALUES; a MISSING secret is Ok with `present: false` — absence is
# a modeled state, not an error. Returns the text as a `String`;
# prefer `secret(name)`, which keeps it a `Secret`.
public tool secret_read(name: String) -> Result<SecretReadEnvelope, String> uses secrets_read

public agent secret_present(name: String, value: String) -> SecretReadEnvelope:
    return SecretReadEnvelope(name, true, value, false, effect_envelope("std.secrets.read", "", "secrets.read", "", "std.secrets.read"))

public agent secret_missing(name: String) -> SecretReadEnvelope:
    return SecretReadEnvelope(name, false, "", false, effect_envelope("std.secrets.read", "", "secrets.read", "", "std.secrets.read"))
